    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eZucchini is a summer buy.\u003c/strong\u003e In season it is one of the cheapest vegetables on the shelf. Out of season it is one of the most expensive. Make this pot when the price is right and it drops a good bit.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBread crumbs are worth making, not buying.\u003c/strong\u003e Heels and stale slices, dried in a low oven and pulsed, cost you nothing and bind meatballs exactly the same way.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy potatoes and carrots in bags.\u003c/strong\u003e Loose produce is priced for people buying two. You are buying for 14 servings, so the bag price wins every time.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned diced tomatoes carry the broth.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy them by the case on sale. They keep for years and this pot goes through a stack of them."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Mix the ground turkey with the eggs, bread crumbs, uncooked rice, minced garlic, dried oregano, ground cumin, salt and black pepper, then roll it into meatballs about the size of a golf ball.",
                    "Brown the meatballs on a sheet pan in a hot oven, around 400F for 15 minutes, so they hold together when they hit the broth.",
                    "Heat the vegetable oil in your big pot and cook the diced onion until soft, then add the carrots and celery and give them a few minutes.",
                    "Pour in the diced tomatoes with their juice and the chicken broth, bring to a simmer, and add the cubed potatoes.",
                    "Slide the meatballs in gently and simmer 20 minutes, until the rice inside them has swelled and the potatoes are tender.",
                    "Add the chopped zucchini and simmer just 5 more minutes so it stays firm, then stir in the chopped cilantro off the heat."
                ],
